{
  "summary": "The UI largely follows the DESIGN.md, but the primary backup flow is broken, several secondary states are missing or incomplete, and a few accessibility and token‑usage details need attention. The biggest blocker is the missing `createBackup` implementation that prevents the \"Backup ready to share\" screen from ever appearing. Other issues are medium‑severity gaps (error UI for policy acceptance, missing focus‑visible outlines, bottom‑tab persistence on modal screens) and low‑severity polish items (autocomplete/kb types on form fields, aria‑live on snackbars, proper alt text, consistent token usage). Fixing the high‑severity backup bug and adding the missing secondary states will bring the product to a polished, production‑ready level.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The backup creation process crashes with \"(0, c.createBackup) is not a function\" and never reaches the success state \"Backup ready to share\". This breaks the primary user flow for exporting data.",
      "fix": "Implement the `createBackup` function in `src/lib/backup.ts` (and export it) and import it correctly in `BackupScreen.tsx`. Add proper async handling, set loading state, and navigate to a success screen or show a success snackbar when the backup is ready."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing success view/state after backup creation. The spec expects a page/dialog that confirms the backup is ready to share, but none is rendered.",
      "fix": "Add a 'BackupSuccessScreen' component (or dialog) that displays the copy \"Backup ready to share\" and a button to share/copy the file. Route to this view after `createBackup` resolves."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "No error UI for the PolicyGateScreen when storing the acceptance fails. The design mandates a full‑screen error view with a Retry button.",
      "fix": "Add an error state to `PolicyScreen` that renders a full‑screen view containing the error message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a `PrimaryButton` labelled \"Retry\" that re‑invokes the acceptance persistence logic."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus outline (2 dp) on web/desktop, violating the spec's focus‑visible requirement.",
      "fix": "Apply a style that adds `outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}` when the button receives focus (e.g., via `onFocus`/`onBlur` or using `:focus-visible` CSS). Ensure the style works for both native and web platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields currently have no `autoComplete` or keyboard type hints; numeric fields like Amount lack `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` and `autoComplete=\"off\"`. This doesn't follow the sign‑up/sign‑in best‑practice checklist (even though the app is offline, the same UX standards apply).",
      "fix": "Pass appropriate `keyboardType` (e.g., `numeric` for amount, `default` for notes) and `autoComplete` props to `TextInput` based on the field's purpose. Add `accessibilityState={{ disabled: disabled }}` for disabled inputs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "The bottom tab bar is not rendered on modal screens such as the backup passphrase dialog, leaving users without a navigation path back to other primary sections.",
      "fix": "Ensure that modal dialogs are rendered within the same navigation hierarchy so the `BottomTabBar` remains visible underneath (e.g., use a portal that does not hide the tab bar) or provide a clear close button that returns to the previous screen. Verify each signed‑in screen includes the tab bar."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Snackbar.tsx",
      "issue": "Snackbars are not marked with `aria-live=\"assertive\"` or `role=\"alert\"`, so screen‑reader users may miss success/error messages.",
      "fix": "Wrap the snackbar content in a component that has `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` (or `aria-live=\"assertive\"` on web) and `role=\"alert\"`. Verify the live region works across platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptImagePicker.tsx",
      "issue": "The receipt thumbnail image lacks an `accessibilityLabel`/`alt` attribute (should be \"Receipt photo\").",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Receipt photo\"` to the Image component (or `alt` on web) to provide descriptive text for assistive technologies."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The illustration in the empty state does not have an `accessibilityLabel` (spec calls for \"Empty state illustration\").",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Empty state illustration\"` to the illustration component and set `importantForAccessibility=\"no\"` if decorative."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen container uses hard‑coded padding values (`16dp`) instead of the design token `spacing*2`. This can cause inconsistency if the token changes.",
      "fix": "Replace literal padding numbers with `theme.spacing * 2` (or a helper like `spacing(2)`) so layout adheres to the token system."
    }
  ]
}

