{
  "summary": "The UI implements the primary flow and passes all axe accessibility checks, with a Lighthouse accessibility score of 98 and no console errors. Navigation works from every signed‑in screen (bottom tab bar is present) and the main states (policy gate, dashboard empty, receipt entry, mileage entry, settings, categories) are reachable. However, a few secondary states and design‑token inconsistencies are missing or incomplete, and some interaction‑state styling (focus outlines) does not fully meet the spec. These issues are not show‑stoppers for the core flow but should be fixed to reach a truly polished product.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The dashboard loading state (full‑screen centered ActivityIndicator) is defined in DESIGN.md but is never rendered – the screen jumps straight to the empty or populated view.",
      "fix": "Add a conditional render that shows <ActivityIndicator size=\"large\" /> centered when the dashboard data is being fetched, and hide it once data is available."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/CategorySelect.tsx",
      "issue": "The dropdown placeholder text \"Select category\" is hard‑coded instead of using a token or the label prop, and the component does not apply the design token spacing for the menu items.",
      "fix": "Expose a `placeholder` prop that defaults to the token‑based string from DESIGN.md and use `theme.spacing` for menu item padding/margin to stay consistent with the 8 dp grid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Visible focus styling (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`) is missing on web – only the ripple effect appears on native platforms.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` CSS rule (or Paper’s `style` prop) that sets a 2 dp solid outline with `theme.colors.outline` and ensures the outline is also applied when navigating with the keyboard."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom navigation tabs lack explicit `aria-label` and `role=\"navigation\"` attributes on the web, which can hinder screen‑reader navigation despite passing axe.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `BottomNavigation` in a `<nav aria-label=\"Primary navigation\">` element and add `accessibilityLabel`/`accessibilityRole` props to each tab to convey their purpose to assistive tech."
